<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">

<div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Professional partition wall installation for offices, retail, and homes across Edinburgh. Metal stud and timber options, sound-rated and fire-rated, with Scottish Building Standards compliance and 12-month guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Partition Wall Services</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Partition walls are one of the fastest and most affordable ways to divide open-plan spaces into functional rooms. At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we design and install partition walls using both timber and metal stud framing, with plasterboard finishes that look clean and professional across Edinburgh's diverse property types.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh's property landscape — from Georgian townhouses in New Town and Stockbridge to modern office blocks in St Andrew Square and the Leith Waterfront, plus residential properties across Morningside, Bruntsfield, Marchmont, and Portobello — demands versatile partition solutions. Whether you need a single room division in a student flat on King Street, an open-plan office layout in the New Town, or a full commercial build-out in the Leith Waterfront regeneration zone, our experienced team delivers on time and on budget.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Standard single-layer plasterboard partitions</li>
  <li>Double-layer soundproof partitions with acoustic insulation</li>
  <li>Fire-rated partitions (30–120 minutes)</li>
  <li>Metal stud partitions for commercial fit-outs</li>
  <li>Timber stud partitions for residential projects</li>
  <li>Demountable and relocatable partitions</li>
  <li>Integrated door and glazing frames</li>
  <li>Corner bead and professional joint finishing</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Our Partition Walls?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Fast and cost-effective:</strong> Partition walls are significantly cheaper and faster to install than traditional brick or block walls, with minimal disruption to your Edinburgh property or business operations.</li>
  <li><strong>Flexible and adaptable:</strong> Unlike permanent walls, partition walls can be modified, extended, or removed as your needs change — ideal for Edinburgh's dynamic commercial property market.</li>
  <li><strong>Sound-rated options:</strong> We install acoustic insulation and sound-rated plasterboard (including British Gypsum SoundBloc and Knauf Acoustic boards) to create quiet, private spaces in offices and homes.</li>
  <li><strong>Fire-rated compliance:</strong> Our fire-rated partitions meet Part B Scottish Building Standards for commercial and public buildings, with full certification documentation provided.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional finish:</strong> Every partition is finished with corner beads, tape, and jointing compound for a seamless surface ready for painting or wallpapering — indistinguishable from plastered walls.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials & Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use high-quality materials from leading UK manufacturers to ensure your partition walls are strong, compliant, and built to last.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Galvanised steel C-studs and U-tracks (50mm, 70mm, 92mm profiles)</li>
  <li>Sawn timber studs for residential partitions (treated 45mm × 47mm)</li>
  <li>British Gypsum Gyproc plasterboard (standard, moisture-resistant, fire-rated, SoundBloc)</li>
  <li>Knauf plasterboard and jointing systems</li>
  <li>Rockwool and Isover acoustic insulation batts (40mm, 50mm, 75mm)</li>
  <li>Fire-rated intumescent sealants and cavity barriers</li>
  <li>Steel corner beads and edge trim</li>
  <li>Joint compound and paper tape for seamless finishing</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications & Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our partition wall services cover a wide range of building types and project sizes across Edinburgh.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Office space division and room creation in the New Town, Stockbridge, and St Andrew Square</li>
  <li>Retail store fitting and back-of-house areas on Princes Street and St James Centre</li>
  <li>Residential room division and extensions in Morningside, Bruntsfield, and Marchmont</li>
  <li>Warehouse and industrial unit partitioning in Leith and Portobello</li>
  <li>Healthcare facility room separation for NHS Lothian and private clinics</li>
  <li>School and education building interiors across Edinburgh Council areas</li>
  <li>Studio and workshop space configuration in the West End and Leith</li>
  <li>Student accommodation and HMO conversions throughout the city</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">How It Works</h2>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Free Quote:</strong> Call or fill in our form. We will assess your space, discuss your layout needs, and provide a detailed, no-obligation quote for your Edinburgh project.</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Plan:</strong> We confirm stud type, board specification, insulation, and any door or glazing integrations. Everything is agreed upfront with full Scottish Building Standards compliance documentation.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional Installation:</strong> Our CSCS-registered team installs the framing, fixes plasterboard, and completes all joints and finishing to a professional standard.</li>
  <li><strong>Quality Check & Handover:</strong> We inspect every partition for straightness and finish quality, provide full compliance documentation, and leave your site clean and ready for decoration.</li>
</ol>

