<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Partition Walls</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is a partition wall?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A partition wall is a non-load-bearing interior wall used to divide open spaces into separate rooms or areas. Partition walls are lightweight, cost-effective, and can be modified or removed in the future.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How much does partition wall installation cost in Edinburgh?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Partition wall costs depend on size, materials, and any acoustic or fire-rating requirements. Single-layer partitions start from around £45-£65 per square metre. We provide free, detailed quotes for every project.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can partition walls be soundproofed?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We install acoustic insulation within the partition cavity and can use double-layer plasterboard with acoustic boards to achieve excellent sound reduction for offices, bedrooms, and meeting rooms.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Are partition walls fire-rated?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. When combined with fire-rated plasterboard, partition walls can achieve fire ratings from 30 minutes up to 120 minutes, meeting Part B building regulation requirements.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How long does it take to install a partition wall?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A single partition wall takes 1-2 days. Multiple partitions or complex layouts may take 3-5 days. We provide accurate timelines during your quote.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can partition walls include doors and windows?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We can integrate standard and fire-rated doors, glazing panels, and sliding doors into partition wall systems to create fully functional rooms.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What areas do you cover for partition walls in Edinburgh?</h3>
